Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 02/04/2025]
1. Resonance energies are adopted from ENSDF 1990.
2. Er = 243 - 486 keV: resonance strengths are the averages of the values given in Table 1 of Goerres et al. 1990. 
3. Er = 495, 597 keV: partial widths adopted from Szuecs & Mohr 2015.
4. Er = 1086, 1231 keV: partial widths adopted from Torres-Sanchez et al. 2023 and Mughabghab 2018.
5. Er = 1408 keV: partial widths adopted from Table 15.11 in Ajzenberg-Selove 1991; the gamma-ray width represents the ground-state width only (see comment in 
   Ajzenberg-Selove 1991).
6. The direct capture S factor has been estimated using experimental C2S values from Bommer et al. 1975, Sercely et al. 1979, and Ruziev et al. 2024.
